# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RivalRadar frontend configuration
#
# NOTHING SECRET BELONGS IN THIS FILE.
#
# Every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value is compiled into the JavaScript bundle and is
# readable by anyone who opens the site. The OpenRouter API key lives only in
# the BACKEND environment (backend/.env locally, Render's dashboard in
# production) and is never sent to the browser. The frontend never talks to
# OpenRouter — it only ever calls the RivalRadar API.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Local development -----------------------------------------------------
# Both values below are OPTIONAL locally. With no .env file at all the
# dashboard works against a backend on http://127.0.0.1:8000, which is what
# `uvicorn app.main:app --reload` gives you.

# Where the Next dev server proxies /api/* on the SERVER side. The browser
# calls same-origin /api/..., so there is no CORS and no backend host in the
# bundle. Change this only if your backend runs elsewhere.
BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# --- Production (GitHub Pages) ---------------------------------------------
# A static export has no proxy, so the browser must call the backend
# directly. REQUIRED for `npm run build:static` — the build fails without it
# rather than shipping a site that 404s on every request.
#
# Your Render URL, no trailing slash:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://rivalradar-api.onrender.com
#
# Whatever origin serves this site must also appear in the backend's
# CORS_ORIGINS, or the browser will block every response.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=

# Base path for a GitHub PROJECT site served from a subdirectory:
#   https://<username>.github.io/<repo>/   ->  NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=/<repo>
#
# Leave EMPTY for a user site (https://<username>.github.io) or a custom
# domain. The deploy workflow sets this automatically from the repository
# name, so you normally do not set it by hand.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=
